# Broad crown (#635, D162): the decor kind `crown-broad`, native 224x128, one frame, hung from the room top; its
# trunk stands under the frame's middle (trunk object x = crown x + 104). A wide dome of big leaf clumps, a lumpy underside
# that hangs lower on the left, and an open bay under the middle where the trunk parts into two limbs around a leader.
# Limbs copied from hand-typed stamps. Palette: D120 leaf green (contour k 1b291b, leaves d m l, olive tips n),
# each clump lit from above (p 2e4030, o 35492f toward the moon) and shadowed underneath (q 141f14); bark keys; no ink, no violet.
# `leaves` (#593, D163): the wind's glints light the leaf keys m, l, n below row 8 (the rows above are over the floor camera's
# top edge); the lit tops p and o, the contour, the shades d and q and the bark stay dark (tools/wind_spots.py).
# Re-arranged (D162, round 4): inside the same silhouette, 9 to 12 big leaf masses of different sizes and tufted shapes at
# irregular offsets, each lit on top (o, p) and shaded toward its underside and its left (away from the moon), deep shadow q
# in the gaps, a contour k round the crown and a dark seam inside its left edge. Drafted in a scratch helper, kept as typed.
size 224 128
color q 141f14
color k 1b291b
color d 202e20
color m 233223
color l 273627
color n 2f301e
color p 2e4030
color o 35492f
color f 220e09
color e 28130e
color b 2e1813
color c 39231d
color h 47302a
color i 454339
frame crown-broad
leaves 0 8 224 120
